Figure 5 illustrates that Nano-11 significantly enhances the transport of antigens to draining lymph nodes and targets them more efficiently to migratory dendritic cells (MigDCs) compared to soluble OVA or OVA adjuvanted with aluminum hydroxide (AH). Flow cytometry data show that Nano-11-adjuvanted OVA leads to a higher mean fluorescence intensity of OVA in antigen-presenting cells, indicating increased antigen uptake per cell. Furthermore, a greater percentage of OVA-positive cells in the draining lymph nodes are MigDCs when formulated with Nano-11, particularly on day 2 post-injection, highlighting its specific targeting capability to these potent antigen-presenting cells.